  "result": "All nine tests pass across both test files.\n\nChanges in `reports/render.py`:\n\n- **Added the `csv` format.** It writes the header row and data rows through the standard library `csv` writer, so cells containing commas or quotes are escaped correctly. No title line.\n- **Added the `html` format.** It emits the heading, opening table tag, a header row of `th` cells, one `td` row per data row, and the closing tag, each on its own line. Cell and title text is HTML-escaped.\n- **Added `render_many`.** It renders each report in order with the given format and returns the list of strings. An unknown format raises `UnknownFormat` on the first report, same as `render`.\n- **Renderers now return a string instead of a list of lines,** and output no longer ends in a trailing newline. The new batch test expects exact output without one, and the text format still keeps its blank line after the title when there are no rows, so the earlier tests are unaffected.",
